### Topic 54 - File Upload, Download and Emails
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### Copy a "storedName" from an upload response into @stored below to try download/view/delete.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@stored = PASTE_STORED_NAME_HERE

### 1) Upload ONE file (multipart/form-data). "< ./sample-files/hello.txt" = read the file from disk.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=CourseBoundary

--CourseBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hello.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./sample-files/hello.txt
--CourseBoundary--

### 2) Upload an image
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=CourseBoundary

--CourseBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="green-dot.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample-files/green-dot.png
--CourseBoundary--

### 3) Upload SEVERAL files - same part name "files"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files/batch
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=CourseBoundary

--CourseBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="hello.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./sample-files/hello.txt
--CourseBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="prices.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./sample-files/prices.csv
--CourseBoundary--

### 4) Forbidden type -> 400 "Upload rejected"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/files
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=CourseBoundary

--CourseBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="evil.html"
Content-Type: text/html

<script>alert('hi')</script>
--CourseBoundary--

### 5) List files
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files

### 6) Download (Content-Disposition: attachment)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files/{{stored}}

### 7) View inline (images / PDF)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files/{{stored}}/view

### 8) Delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/files/{{stored}}

### 9) Plain-text email (start Mailpit first: docker compose up -d, inbox http://localhost:8025)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/emails/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "asha@example.com",
  "subject": "Your order has shipped",
  "text": "Hi Asha,\nyour order #1001 is on its way.\n\nThanks, Shop Team"
}

### 10) HTML email with an uploaded file as attachment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/emails/with-attachment
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "asha@example.com",
  "subject": "Your invoice",
  "html": "<h1>Thank you!</h1><p>Your invoice is <b>attached</b>.</p>",
  "storedFileName": "{{stored}}"
}

### 11) Invalid email address -> 400 from @Valid
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/emails/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "not-an-email",
  "subject": "x",
  "text": "y"
}
